  "candidates": [
    {
      "key": "implementation_role",
      "source_path": null,
      "role": "Requirement",
      "form": "Declaration",
      "summary": "Declare Implementation Role",
      "main_subject": "CAPRMEDIO_MODEL <+ Atom/(.Header.Role := Implementation)",
      "body": "## Summary\n\nDeclare Implementation Role\n\n## Claim\n\n### Formal Claim\n\n```CFEL\n# model\nAtom/(.Header.Role := Implementation)\n```\n\n## Semantics\n\nAn Implementation Atom describes actual implementation: code parts, behavior, structure and rationale. A specification is optional. Supported facts and inferred explanations remain distinguishable. A specification difference is a neutral observation; assessment determines whether it requires resolution as a Concern.\n"
    },
    {
      "key": "code_synopsis_form",
      "source_path": null,
      "role": "Requirement",
      "form": "Declaration",
      "summary": "Declare Code Synopsis Form",
      "main_subject": "CAPRMEDIO_MODEL <+ Atom/(.Header.Form := Code Synopsis)",
      "body": "## Summary\n\nDeclare Code Synopsis Form\n\n## Claim\n\n### Formal Claim\n\n```CFEL\n# model\nAtom/(.Header.Form := Code Synopsis);\n\n# instances\nAtom/(.Header.Form := Code Synopsis)//$synopsis.Header.Role:: [in (Implementation)]{::1}\n```\n\n## Semantics\n\nA Code Synopsis is a concise, structured explanation of actual code, including its behavior, structure and rationale. It supports code without a specification.\n"
    }
  ],
